  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "A particle is projected from the origin with initial speed $20\\sqrt{2}$ m/s. On its flight it passes through the point $(20,15)$ at time $t$. Let $\\theta$ be the angle of projection.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta=1$ and $4\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta-t^2=3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta=1$, $4\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta-t^2=3$.",
          "worked": "Using $g=10\\text{ m s}^{-2}$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}x&=20\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta\\\\20&=20\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta\\\\\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta&=1.\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=-5t^2+20\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta\\\\15&=-5t^2+20\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta\\\\4\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta-t^2&=3.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence show that $\\tan^2\\theta-8\\tan\\theta+7=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\tan^2\\theta-8\\tan\\theta+7=0$.",
          "worked": "From $\\sqrt{2}t\\cos\\theta=1$,\n$$t=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta}.$$\nSubstitute into $4\\sqrt{2}t\\sin\\theta-t^2=3$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta}\\right)\\sin\\theta-\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}\\cos\\theta}\\right)^2&=3\\\\4\\tan\\theta-\\frac12\\sec^2\\theta&=3\\\\8\\tan\\theta-(1+\\tan^2\\theta)&=6\\\\\\tan^2\\theta-8\\tan\\theta+7&=0.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 39
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence find, to the nearest minute where necessary, the two possible values of $\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $81^\\circ52'$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}(\\tan\\theta-1)(\\tan\\theta-7)&=0\\\\\\tan\\theta&=1\\text{ or }7\\\\\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }\\tan^{-1}(7)\\\\\\theta&=45^\\circ\\text{ or }81^\\circ52'\\quad\\text{(nearest minute).}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      }
    ]
  },
